# Gmail search with gws

Read-only skill. Do not send, delete, or modify mail unless the user explicitly asks.

## Prerequisites

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} auth status
```

## Choose the right command

| Need | Command |
|------|---------|
| Human-readable table (sender, subject, date) | `{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage --query '...'` |
| JSON for scripting / jq | add `--format json` |
| Message IDs only, large result sets | `users messages list` API (see below) |
| Full message body | `{{ gws_bin }} gmail +read --id ID --headers` |
| List label names/IDs | `{{ gws_bin }} gmail users labels list --params '{"userId":"me"}'` |

## Gmail query cheat sheet

Combine fragments with spaces (implicit AND).

| Goal | Query fragment | Example |
|------|----------------|---------|
| Sent mail | `in:sent` | `in:sent newer_than:7d` |
| Inbox only | `in:inbox` | `in:inbox is:unread` |
| Label | `label:NAME` | `label:work` |
| Last N days | `newer_than:Nd` | `newer_than:14d` (also `1d`, `30d`, `90d`) |
| After date | `after:YYYY/MM/DD` | `after:2026/06/01` |
| Before date | `before:YYYY/MM/DD` | `before:2026/07/01` |
| From sender | `from:email` | `from:alice@example.com` |
| To recipient | `to:email` | `to:team@company.com` |
| Cc | `cc:email` | `cc:manager@company.com` |
| Subject | `subject:word` | `subject:invoice` |
| Body / anywhere | bare words | `quarterly report` |
| Exact phrase | `"..."` | `"project alpha"` |
| Unread | `is:unread` | `is:unread from:boss` |
| Read | `is:read` | `is:read label:archive` |
| Starred | `is:starred` | `is:starred newer_than:30d` |
| Has attachment | `has:attachment` | `has:attachment from:vendor` |
| Exclude label | `-label:X` | `in:inbox -label:spam` |
| OR | `{a b}` | `from:alice OR from:bob` → `{from:alice from:bob}` |

## Workflow: sent in last X days with label Y

Replace `Y` with the label name and `X` with the day count.

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage \
  --query 'in:sent label:Y newer_than:Xd' \
  --max 100 --labels
```

Example — all mail sent in the last 14 days labeled `work`:

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage \
  --query 'in:sent label:work newer_than:14d' \
  --max 100 --labels --format table
```

JSON output for further processing:

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage \
  --query 'in:sent label:work newer_than:14d' \
  --max 100 --format json
```

## Workflow: search by keyword, sender, or subject

```bash
# Keyword anywhere
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage --query 'quarterly budget' --max 50

# From specific sender, last week
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage --query 'from:client@corp.com newer_than:7d' --max 50

# Subject line
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage --query 'subject:invoice newer_than:30d' --max 50

# Unread in inbox from boss
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +triage --query 'is:unread from:boss@company.com' --max 20
```

## Workflow: read full messages after search

1. Run `+triage` or `messages list` to get message IDs.
2. Read each message:

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +read --id MESSAGE_ID --headers
{{ gws_bin }} gmail +read --id MESSAGE_ID --format json | jq '.body'
```

## API: list message IDs (pagination)

Use when you need more than 100 results or raw API output:

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} gmail users messages list \
  --params '{"userId": "me", "q": "in:sent label:work newer_than:7d", "maxResults": 500}' \
  --format json
```

Auto-paginate (NDJSON, one page per line):

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} gmail users messages list \
  --params '{"userId": "me", "q": "label:work newer_than:30d", "maxResults": 100}' \
  --page-all --page-limit 10
```

Inspect schema for any method:

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} schema gmail.users.messages.list
```

## Label tips

- Label names with spaces: `label:"my label"` or `label:my-label`
- List all labels to verify exact names:

```bash
{{ gws_bin }} gmail users labels list \
  --params '{"userId": "me"}' --format table
```

## Presenting results to the user

Default `+triage` output is a table — show it directly.
For JSON, summarize: count, top senders/subjects, date range.
Offer to `+read` specific messages if the user wants bodies.

